    "notes": "Complete mapped granary/Житня exterior at Yasnaya Polyana: timber-supported two-storey storehouse with log lower walls, weathered vertical-board upper room, broad low hip roof over an open front gallery and an external stair descending along the front. Lower double wooden gate and upper doorway are physically recessed; short-side vent, timber posts, open rails, stringers and supported entrance/foot aprons remain simple original proxies. All four mapped outer edges anchor the house/gallery envelope. Hidden rear inventory, roof material and historic levels remain approximate. No copied signs, merchandise, inscriptions, artworks, furnishings, people, snow or photograph pixels. Photo-led approximate medium-fi scale: lower room2.25m, upper room2.05m, low hip roof1.5m rise. Gallery at2.25m has simple.92m open rails;12 treads descend along the front. Map nominal5m is a scale cue. Rear bays, historical cladding/roof state, timber frame sections, doors, treads, thresholds and accessibility are not surveyed. Retained Protomaps20261020 and Mapzen201x201/6m ground; outside northeast approach provider[0,7] supplies224.57842704651677m datum. Boundary grades-0.993..0.254m, floor+0.5m and timber pier bottoms-1.2m. The coarse slope leaves up to about1.5m below the downhill floor; the original ground remains beneath the raised rooms, gallery and stair. Only occupied pier feet and the two supported aprons cut the ground. Historic support exposure/levels and accessibility approximate; no flattening or bespoke terrain. Independent neighbors, approaches, roads and ponds remain. The photographs partly obscure the roof and footings with trees/snow. A shared weathered cedar-shingle graph approximates the unresolved roof finish; no snow or photograph pixels are copied. Hidden rear inventory and absolute front assignment remain a photo/map interpretation. Fixed synthetic planes partly bury the grade-specific supports/aprons; whole native/turntable views cover the envelope. Other